const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"先问模型能识别什么",en:"Start with what the test can identify"},body:{zh:"论文比较多种应计模型的检验表现，而不是给每家公司贴上操纵标签。检验既可能把没有发生的系统性管理误判为存在，也可能漏掉真实变化。阅读结果时，应同时关注误报与检出能力，不能把一次显著性检验当成独立的事实认定。",en:"The paper compares accrual-based tests, not company misconduct labels. A test may reject a true null or miss an actual intervention. Its rejection rate and detection power answer different questions; statistical significance alone does not establish the underlying conduct."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第193–195页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 193–195"}}},{title:{zh:"残差里不只有管理裁量",en:"A residual contains more than discretion"},body:{zh:"可操纵应计无法直接观察，需要从总应计中估计正常部分。如果遗漏的经营因素与研究事件相关，剩余项也会带上这种相关性。反过来，过强的控制可能吸收本来想寻找的变化。因此残差大小必须结合模型设定理解，而不是直接解释为操纵金额。",en:"Discretionary accruals are unobserved. Estimating normal accruals leaves measurement error alongside the intended component. Omitted operating factors correlated with an event can bias inference, while controls may absorb the intervention being studied. The residual is not a directly observed manipulation amount."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第195–198页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 195–198"}}},{title:{zh:"修正发生在事件期的收入变量",en:"The modification changes event-period revenue"},body:{zh:"原Jones模型用收入变化和固定资产等变量解释正常应计。修正版在事件期从收入变化中扣除应收账款变化，两项均按上期总资产缩放。参数仍从原Jones估计期模型取得；不要把这一版本默认为每个年度都重新估计的行业横截面模型。",en:"The original Jones model uses revenue changes and property, plant and equipment. Its modified version subtracts the change in receivables from event-period revenue changes, both scaled by lagged assets. Parameters still come from the original estimation-period model, not an automatically substituted annual industry cross-section."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第198–199页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 198–199"}}},{title:{zh:"赊销假设需要单独审视",en:"Examine the credit-sales assumption"},body:{zh:"这一修正针对收入确认裁量被原模型当成正常收入变化吸收的问题，但隐含假设是事件期赊销变化来自盈余管理。实际企业也可能因客户结构、收款周期或业务增长增加应收款。理解假设的强度，比机械套用“修正后更准确”更重要。",en:"The adjustment targets revenue discretion absorbed as normal activity by the original model. It assumes event-period credit-sales changes arise from earnings management. Ordinary changes in customers, collections or growth may also affect receivables, so the assumption needs scrutiny rather than a blanket claim of improved accuracy."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第199页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 199"}}},{title:{zh:"不同样本检验不同问题",en:"Different samples test different weaknesses"},body:{zh:"作者区分随机公司年度、极端业绩样本、人工加入应计变化的样本和监管执法样本。随机抽样主要考察一般情况下的检验设定，极端业绩揭示混淆风险；人工样本的解释依赖操纵方式与转回时点，执法样本也不是所有企业的随机代表。",en:"Random firm-years, extreme-performance samples, injected accrual changes and enforcement cases serve different purposes. Random sampling probes general specification; extreme performance probes confounding. Simulation depends on the intervention and reversal timing, while enforcement cases are not a random cross-section of all firms."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第200–201页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 200–201"}}},{title:{zh:"把显著性放回经营背景",en:"Return significance to its operating context"},body:{zh:"论文提醒研究者，较小幅度的管理可能难以检出，极端业绩下的拒绝率也可能偏离名义水平。实务阅读应先核对经营变化、事件选择与可比期间，再理解异常应计。未检出不能证明没有管理，检出也不能单凭模型断言是谁、为何改变了报表。",en:"Modest interventions may be difficult to detect, and rejection rates can behave differently under extreme performance. Interpret estimates alongside operating changes, event selection and comparable periods. Failure to reject does not establish absence, and rejection does not by itself identify an actor or motive."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2308/tar-9505096112",label:{zh:"原文定位：1995年期刊版，第193–195, 201页",en:"Source: 1995 journal article, pp. 193–195, 201"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"异常应计是模型估计量，不是违规认定。本文比较的是特定样本与模拟条件下的检验表现；业绩、收入确认和模型误差都可能影响推断。",en:"Abnormal accruals are model estimates, not findings of misconduct. Test performance depends on the sampled firms and simulated mechanisms; performance, revenue recognition and measurement error affect inference."}};export{e as default};
